# warnings

## DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY

```text
[DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY] The external module "ext-inner" evaluates when its chunk loads, not when the deferred module evaluates. "main.js" defers "d.js", and "inner.js" in the dependencies of "d.js" imports "ext-inner". ESM output loads each external module at the start of the chunk that imports it. To evaluate "ext-inner" lazily, bundle it, or use the CommonJS output format, which loads it with `require()` in the deferred code. CommonJS output works only when the runtime supports CommonJS and the module can load with `require()`.

```

## DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY

```text
[DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY] The external module "ext-lazy" evaluates when its chunk loads, not when the deferred module evaluates. "main.js" defers "d.js", and "d.js" imports "ext-lazy". ESM output loads each external module at the start of the chunk that imports it. To evaluate "ext-lazy" lazily, bundle it, or use the CommonJS output format, which loads it with `require()` in the deferred code. CommonJS output works only when the runtime supports CommonJS and the module can load with `require()`.

```

# Assets

## main.js

```js
import "ext-eager";
import "ext-inner";
import { value } from "ext-lazy";
import { join } from "node:path";
// HIDDEN [\0rolldown/runtime.js]
// inner.js
function init_inner() {
	return (init_inner = __esmMin((() => {})))();
}
// d.js
var x;
function init_d() {
	return (init_d = __esmMin((() => {
		init_inner();
		x = [value, join];
	})))();
}
// main.js
const read = () => (init_d(), x);
export { read };

```

# Variant: [format: Iife] [name: "lib"]

## warnings

### DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY

```text
[DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY] The external module "ext-inner" evaluates when its chunk loads, not when the deferred module evaluates. "main.js" defers "d.js", and "inner.js" in the dependencies of "d.js" imports "ext-inner". IIFE output loads each external module at the start of the chunk that imports it. To evaluate "ext-inner" lazily, bundle it, or use the CommonJS output format, which loads it with `require()` in the deferred code. CommonJS output works only when the runtime supports CommonJS and the module can load with `require()`.

```

### DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY

```text
[DEFERRED_EXTERNAL_EVALUATED_EAGERLY] The external module "ext-lazy" evaluates when its chunk loads, not when the deferred module evaluates. "main.js" defers "d.js", and "d.js" imports "ext-lazy". IIFE output loads each external module at the start of the chunk that imports it. To evaluate "ext-lazy" lazily, bundle it, or use the CommonJS output format, which loads it with `require()` in the deferred code. CommonJS output works only when the runtime supports CommonJS and the module can load with `require()`.

